From: Uke Linux maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: gate Uke thresholds and FCC by reviewed leases

Add default-off Uke-only standard threshold and constant-current interfaces.
Require typed, bounded per-boot admission, current measurements, serialized
requests and exact firmware setting readback. Keep voltage, USB input budget
and negotiation outside this backend. A firmware ACK is not physical success.

OEM ABI comparison: MiCode uke-v-oss 5712080a4b0c and OnePlus fc892483f1d6;
shared implementation: Peridot 2ed9eadbecae and Linux4056b3c9d3c9.
Prepared against project f429992feb63. No build, test or hardware acceptance.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/Kconfig
@@ -217,6 +217,29 @@
 	  which is used on modern Qualcomm platforms to provide battery and
 	  power supply information.
 
+config BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR_UKE_THRESHOLDS
+	bool "Reviewed Uke autonomous charge-threshold transport"
+	depends on BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR && EXPERT
+	default n
+	help
+	  Build the restricted Uke threshold backend. This is not a firmware
+	  qualification. Every operation also requires a privileged, per-source,
+	  expiring admission lease and matching firmware readback. Leave disabled
+	  until the exact active firmware, reply envelope, threshold semantics,
+	  measurement units and autonomous protection evidence are reviewed.
+	  No PD, current, voltage, factory or gauge control is enabled here.
+
+config BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR_UKE_CURRENT
+	bool "Reviewed Uke constant-charge-current transport"
+	depends on BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR_UKE_THRESHOLDS
+	default n
+	help
+	  Build the separately admitted positive constant-current backend for
+	  exact Uke OEM wire property 12. Per-boot evidence must establish its
+	  units, readback, effective behavior and firmware-owned CV/protections.
+	  This does not enable the ambiguous thermal-level property 10, voltage
+	  writes, raw properties, PD negotiation or negative/reset sentinels.
+
 config BATTERY_OLPC
 	tristate "One Laptop Per Child battery"
 	depends on OLPC_EC
