+What:           /sys/bus/auxiliary/devices/*/uke_charge_state
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
+Description:
+                Experimental source candidate for xiaomi,uke only. No firmware
+                I/O. Space-separated version-1 decimal fields (27 tokens):
+                version threshold_compiled lease_live transaction_generation
+                firmware_generation source_generation driver_instance_ns
+                lease_expires_ns feature_enabled raw_start raw_end
+                threshold_readback_valid threshold_readback_ns last_errno
+                standard_clients profile_sha256 current_compiled
+                current_admitted reported_fcc_ua current_readback_valid
+                current_readback_ns battery_temperature_deciC battery_voltage_uv
+                battery_current_ua measurement_begin_ns measurement_valid
+                lifecycle_invalidation_ns
+
+                SHA256 is 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters, or 'none'.
+                Times use CLOCK_BOOTTIME. Generations are local epochs, not
+                remote transaction IDs or authenticated firmware identities.
+                Current is battery-side, Linux positive while charging.
+                Readback validity proves a fresh setting report only, never
+                effective current, electrical cutoff, safety or persistence.
+                Measurement age is from the beginning of the complete guard.
+                Standard power_supply properties are cached only, return
+                -ENODATA without a valid admitted standard-client lease, and
+                require the dedicated kernel options (both default n).
+
+What:           /sys/bus/auxiliary/devices/*/uke_charge_lease
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
+Description:
+                CAP_SYS_ADMIN, write only, no firmware I/O. Exact grammar:
+                1 instance generation firmware source expires ack_bytes usb_type
+                  may_change_feature standard_clients min_deciC max_deciC
+                  min_battery_uv max_battery_uv abs_battery_current_ua
+                  cap_resume_percent profile_sha256 reviewed_boottime_ns
+
+                The 18 tokens are on one line. Values must match current driver
+                epochs. Lease <=30 seconds; owner is a referenced TGID (not its
+                reusable numeric PID). Other owners cannot renew a live lease.
+                Only explicitly admitted root standard clients can borrow it.
+                Reviewed time must follow the most recent suspend/PDR
+                invalidation; old evidence cannot auto-resume after suspend.
+                Source changes require matching fresh per-boot attestation.
+                Guards and ACK length require exact reviewed firmware evidence.
+                No shipped profile supplies qualified limits or identities.
+                Write 'revoke' by the owner to remove software permission.
+                Revocation, process failure and expiry do NOT undo a setting,
+                restore OEM defaults or physically stop charging.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/auxiliary/devices/*/uke_charge_thresholds
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
+Description:
+                CAP_SYS_ADMIN plus live qualified lease; write START END with
+                0<=START<END<=100. Fresh health/presence/V/I/T and online USB
+                type must satisfy the reviewed profile. Reads firmware feature
+                enable/start/end (wire25/26/27). If explicitly admitted, feature
+                enable uses wire25 SET. Opcode0x48 carries end and end-start.
+                Exact ACK envelope and subsequent exact GETs are mandatory.
+                Any transport/generation/readback error propagates. No replay.
+                Pair0/100 disables the threshold feature through wire25; it
+                does not enable a zero-start hysteresis or assert cutoff.
+                The two standard charge_control_*_threshold attributes use
+                the same guarded implementation but remain separate writes.
+                A failure of the second standard write may leave the first
+                applied. No transactional rollback or persistence is promised.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/auxiliary/devices/*/uke_charge_refresh
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
+Description:
+                CAP_SYS_ADMIN plus live lease. Write1 for guarded firmware
+                GETs and cached readback renewal; no firmware SET. It reads FCC
+                wire12 only after explicit current-envelope admission. Errors
+                invalidate reported freshness and propagate without retry.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/auxiliary/devices/*/uke_charge_current_profile
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
+Description:
+                CAP_SYS_ADMIN and exact lease-owner TGID only; no firmware I/O.
+                Requires CONFIG_BATTERY_QCOM_BATTMGR_UKE_CURRENT. Grammar:
+                1 profile_sha256 min_ua max_ua source_budget_battery_ua band_count
+                  [min_deciC max_deciC max_ua max_battery_uv]...
+                One line, 1..8 ascending nonoverlapping half-open bands inside
+                the lease limits. All positive FCC limits use microamperes;
+                max_ua=0 for a band inhibits software changes, not charging.
+                Source budget is a qualified BATTERY-SIDE budget after losses
+                and system load, never a copied USB input-current limit.
+
+What:           /sys/bus/auxiliary/devices/*/uke_charge_current_ua
+Date:           October 2026
+Contact:        Uke Linux maintainers
+Description:
+                CAP_SYS_ADMIN plus live current admission. Positive uA only.
+                Fresh guard, matching thermal band, battery voltage, source
+                budget and pack limits apply before wire12 SET; exact wire12
+                GET readback follows. An increase while discharging is denied.
+                Standard constant_charge_current uses this implementation.
+                No wire10 thermal-level setter, negative/UINT_MAX reset, voltage,
+                Xiaomi raw property, USB current, PD/QC/PPS/EPR negotiation or
+                factory/calibration API is exposed. Firmware owns CV and all
+                autonomous protections. This driver is not a real-time cutoff.
